      "content": "The permanence of the damage is what makes this so incredibly heavy, and that weight is suffocating. You are not a stain; you are a person who made a terrible choice, and that's a distinction that matters. If you truly believe your existence is inherently wrong, then the only honest thing left is to find a way to stop the cycle of self-punishment. A small, deliberate act of self-caring, even if it feels futile, is a way to prove to yourself that you are still worth the effort of living.",
